-------------------------------------------------------------------

     =========================================================
     Geant4 - an Object-Oriented Toolkit for Simulation in HEP
     =========================================================

                            TestEmXX
                            --------

	How to compute angular distribution of a gamma interaction with polarization.
	The angular distribution can be calculated in two planes, one is the parallel to
	the polarization of the incident photon and the other is perpendicular to it.
	Polarization of secondary photon is plotted as a function of scattering angle in 	2D histogram. Therefore, polarization transfer can be studied.

 1- GEOMETRY DEFINITION

 	It is a single box representing a 'semi infinite' homogeneous medium.
 	Two parameters define the geometry :
 	- the material of the box,
	- the (full) size of the box.

 	The default geometry (100 m of gold) is constructed in
	DetectorConstruction, but the above parameters can be changed
	interactively via the commands defined in DetectorMessenger.

 2- PHYSICS LIST

 	The physics list contains the standard electromagnetic processes. In addition,
	G4JAEAPolarizedElasticScattering process is included for gammas in order to study
	polarization transfer. For gold, a depolarization is observed at 175 keV, when the
	incident photon has a polarization of 98.01%. See New J Phys. 21, 113006, 2019 
	(https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1367-2630/ab4d8a) for more details.

 3- AN EVENT : THE PRIMARY GENERATOR

 	The primary kinematic consists of a single particle starting at the edge
	of the box. The type of the particle and its energy are set in
	PrimaryGeneratorAction (1 MeV gamma), and can be changed via the G4
 	build-in commands of ParticleGun class (see the macros provided with
 	this example).

 4- PHYSICS

	An event is killed at the first interaction of the incident particle.
	The absorption length, also called mean free path, is computed as
	the mean value of the track length of the incident particle.
	This is why the medium must be 'infinite' : to be sure that interaction
	occurs at any events.

	The plane in which the angular distribution is calculated is selected by the
	azimuth angle (see SteppingAction). The polarization of the incident photon
	can be assigned by macro file. Note that the polarization vector is a
	G4ThreeVector with its components corresponding to Stokes parameters.

 	A set of macros defining various run conditions are provided.
 	The processes are actived/inactived in order to survey the processes
	individually.

 5- HISTOGRAMS

	The test contains 2 built-in 1D histograms, which are managed by the
	HistoManager class and its Messenger. In addition the test contains 1 built-in 2D 	histogram. The histos can be individually activated with the command :
	/analysis/h1/set id nbBins  valMin valMax unit
	/analysis/h2/setX id nbBins  valMin valMax unit
	/analysis/h2/setY id nbBins  valMin valMax unit
	where unit is the desired unit for the histo (MeV or keV, etc..)
	(see the macros gamma.mac).

	1	"Horizontal Theta Distribution"
	2	"Vertical Theta Distribution"
	3	"Polarization of Scattered Photon"


   The histograms are managed by the HistoManager class and its Messenger.
   The histos can be individually activated with the command :
   /analysis/h1/set id nbBins  valMin valMax unit
   where unit is the desired unit for the histo (MeV or keV, deg or mrad, etc..)

   One can control the name of the histograms file with the command:
   /analysis/setFileName  name  (default testemXX)

   It is possible to choose the format of the histogram file : root (default),
   hbook, xml, csv, by using namespace in HistoManager.hh

   It is also possible to print selected histograms on an ascii file:
   /analysis/h1/setAscii id
   All selected histos will be written on a file name.ascii (default testem14)

 Using hbook format
 ------------------

 Need a special treatement : the Cern Library must be installed and the
 environment variable CERNLIB correctly set. Then, *before* compiling,
 activate G4_USE_HBOOK in GNUmakefile and g4hbook.hh in HistoManager.hh

 6- VISUALIZATION

 	The Visualization Manager is set in the main().
 	The initialisation of the drawing is done via the commands
 	/vis/... in the macro vis.mac. To get visualisation:
 	> /control/execute vis.mac

 	The detector has a default view which is a longitudinal view of the
 	box.

 	The tracks are drawn at the end of event, and erased at the end of run.

 7- HOW TO START ?

	execute TestEmXX in 'batch' mode from macro files :
 		% TestEmXX   photon.mac

	execute TestEm14 in 'interactive mode' with visualization :
 		% TestEm14
		Idle> control/execute vis.mac
 		....
 		Idle> type your commands
 		....
 		Idle> exit
